title: The Bookseller
portrait left: seeker
portrait right: bookseller

bookseller: Rare volumes! Rarer than they should be, if you take my meaning.
bookseller: Seventy-five gold for something you have never seen. Or I pay you a hundred to carry something nobody wants.

choice:
  - [if gold >= 75] Buy a random Rare card, 75 gold -> buy
  - Take 100 gold and a Curse -> curse
  - Walk on -> leave

@buy
  > gold -75
  > card add random rare
  bookseller: Handle it carefully. Or don't. It's yours.
  > end

@curse
  > gold 100
  > curse injury
  bookseller: Pleasure doing business. Mind the paper cuts.
  > end

@leave
  bookseller: Suit yourself. The shelves remember who walked past.
  > end
